we have two type of linked list
1.SINGLY
2.DOUBLY

we implement the singly linked list
in doubly linked list, each node has both next and pre node reference
they are bidirectional!

Note: the whole goal of "DOUBLY" linked-list
      is make delete last item runtime complexity to O(1)

Note: the "DOUBLY" linked-list
      need to store more data on each node
      so he has bigger footprint than singly footprint.

Note: JAVA linked-list class is "DOUBLY" !
      so "removeLast()" method from LinkedList is O(1)



CIRCULAR LINKED-LIST
both singly and doubly linked-list can be circular,
in singly linked list, last node should have a pointer to first node
in doubly linked list, last node should have a pointer to first node
                       first node should have a pointer to last node

Note: circular linked-list used for some list
      like play list, when we want to replay the list from beginning
      when we want to iterate on the list!